pression $-\\frac{1}{5}s+2t$ has two terms: $-\\frac{1}{5}s$ and $2t.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n2t-\\frac{1}{5}s.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-583bb0ab-76b5-55bc-9441-2b768b6ea99c" "answer-field-472cde22-93c2-5545-9698-e14f4b892f9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-583bb0ab-76b5-55bc-9441-2b768b6ea99c" :answer-field/id #uuid "583bb0ab-76b5-55bc-9441-2b768b6ea99c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b942be4e-84a6-57ae-993d-c5ce7f403434" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b942be4e-84a6-57ae-993d-c5ce7f403434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b942be4e-84a6-57ae-993d-c5ce7f403434" :answer/id #uuid "b942be4e-84a6-57ae-993d-c5ce7f403434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-472cde22-93c2-5545-9698-e14f4b892f9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "472cde22-93c2-5545-9698-e14f4b892f9a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c35a9517-7fe7-5593-9ef5-67430fa53d2c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c35a9517-7fe7-5593-9ef5-67430fa53d2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c35a9517-7fe7-5593-9ef5-67430fa53d2c" :answer/id #uuid "c35a9517-7fe7-5593-9ef5-67430fa53d2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078914 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $6z+\\frac{3}{2}x+2y+\\frac{5}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression $6z+\\frac{3}{2}x+2y+\\frac{5}{2}$ has four terms:  $6z$, $\\frac{3}{2}x$, $2y$ and $\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n2y+\\frac{5}{2}+6z+\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186076262 :answer-field/correct "answer-835311f0-0bd8-53f0-8bbb-c23df8b44216" :answer-field/choices ["answer-640428b8-1900-50ac-97c7-af250557e759" "answer-835311f0-0bd8-53f0-8bbb-c23df8b44216" "answer-d3a029dd-9b34-57a5-9e78-ba4a2ccd2de8" "answer-22ddd719-e1ba-5276-ae7c-263dda5aa3b5" "answer-5d165dc6-3eca-5638-b1bf-326216f2b83c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-640428b8-1900-50ac-97c7-af250557e759" :answer/id #uuid "640428b8-1900-50ac-97c7-af250557e759" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+4+6z+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-835311f0-0bd8-53f0-8bbb-c23df8b44216" :answer/id #uuid "835311f0-0bd8-53f0-8bbb-c23df8b44216" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+\\frac{5}{2}+6z+\\frac{3}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3a029dd-9b34-57a5-9e78-ba4a2ccd2de8" :answer/id #uuid "d3a029dd-9b34-57a5-9e78-ba4a2ccd2de8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6y+\\frac{3}{2}+2z+\\frac{5}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22ddd719-e1ba-5276-ae7c-263dda5aa3b5" :answer/id #uuid "22ddd719-e1ba-5276-ae7c-263dda5aa3b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+\\frac{5}{2}+z+\\frac{3}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d165dc6-3eca-5638-b1bf-326216f2b83c" :answer/id #uuid "5d165dc6-3eca-5638-b1bf-326216f2b83c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z+4x+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079714 :tutorial/content "Let's take a look at the following algebraic expression:\n\n$$\n2x{\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} 7\n$$\n\nThe addition $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ and subtraction $({\\color{red}{-}})$ symbols separate this expression into three parts known as **terms**.  \n\nTo identify each term, we put an addition symbol $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2x) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} ({\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} (7).\n$$\n\nSo, the terms of this expression are: \n\n$$\n2x,\\quad -4y,\\quad  \\quad 7\n$$\n\nWe say that $2x$ is the **first term**, $-4y$ is the **second term**, and $7$ is the **third term**. \n\nIn this example, the subtraction symbol gave us the term $-4y$. Whenever there is a subtraction symbol, the corresponding term will be negative." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079715 :tutorial/content "When two algebraic expressions contain exactly the same terms, they are said to be **equivalent**.\n\nFor example, the expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}} + 3z\n$$\n\nis equivalent to \n\n$$\n3z+{\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}}\n$$\n\nbecause they both contain the exact same terms. Both expressions are also equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{x}} + 3z+ {\\color{red}{2y}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078665 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
